<title>USA: Crossmann buys Kentucky building company.</title>
<headline>Crossmann buys Kentucky building company.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crossmann Communities Inc said Friday it acquired Cutter Homes Ltd, a home building company in Lexington, Kentucky.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Cutter sold 119 new homes averaging $121,800 in its fiscal year ended April 30. As of today, it has a sales backlog of 45 homes.</p>
<p>Crossmann is a regional builder of single-family homes.</p>
<p>	    ((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
